WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.501
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:09.025
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:15.901
Unit fifteen: Modals of Possibility (might/could). Today you will guess and talk about things that are possible.

4
00:00:16.201 --> 00:00:18.633
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:23.078
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:24.674
Might.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:27.962
Might means used for a weak possibility.

8
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.679
It might rain.

9
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:32.611
Your turn. Say: Might.

10
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.340
Might.

11
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:37.875
Could.

12
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:40.999
Could means used for a possibility.

13
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:42.712
She could be late.

14
00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:45.609
Your turn. Say: Could.

15
00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.073
Could.

16
00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:50.562
May.

17
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.968
May means used for a formal possibility.

18
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:55.759
It may snow.

19
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.410
Your turn. Say: May.

20
00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:02.059
May.

21
00:01:02.817 --> 00:01:03.980
Possibility.

22
00:01:04.983 --> 00:01:07.540
Possibility means something that can happen.

23
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.708
There is a possibility.

24
00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:13.120
Your turn. Say: Possibility.

25
00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:16.991
Possibility.

26
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:18.681
Uncertain.

27
00:01:19.683 --> 00:01:21.439
Uncertain means not sure.

28
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.341
I am uncertain.

29
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.544
Your turn. Say: Uncertain.

30
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.471
Uncertain.

31
00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:32.276
Perhaps.

32
00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:34.726
Perhaps means maybe.

33
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:36.736
Perhaps he is busy.

34
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.886
Your turn. Say: Perhaps.

35
00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:43.827
Perhaps.

36
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:45.492
Guess.

37
00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:48.831
Guess means to give an answer without knowing.

38
00:01:49.417 --> 00:01:50.778
Guess what he is doing.

39
00:01:51.383 --> 00:01:53.943
Your turn. Say: Guess.

40
00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.662
Guess.

41
00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.360
Likely.

42
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.978
Likely means probable.

43
00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:03.747
Rain is likely.

44
00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.304
Your turn. Say: Likely.

45
00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.179
Likely.

46
00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:15.757
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.617 --> 00:02:19.115
Visal, what might your friend be doing right now?

48
00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:30.430
She might be studying, or she could be having dinner. Might and could show that I am not sure. They are for possibilities in the present or future.

49
00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:32.796
Is may the same?

50
00:02:33.883 --> 00:02:44.723
Almost. May is a little more formal: It may rain later. For a strong feeling, we use must or can't, but might, could and may mean only maybe.

51
00:02:45.817 --> 00:02:47.038
What about the negative?

52
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:57.641
Might not and may not are fine: He might not come. But could not usually means he was unable, so for a guess we prefer might not.

53
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.625
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.483 --> 00:03:05.851
Grammar focus: Modals of possibility: might and could and may.

55
00:03:06.151 --> 00:03:07.269
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.983 --> 00:03:09.623
She might be studying now.

57
00:03:10.517 --> 00:03:11.901
It could rain tomorrow.

58
00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:14.607
He might not come to the party.

59
00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:22.181
Might, could and may mean 'maybe'. Use base verb after them. For a guess in the negative use might not, not could not.

60
00:03:22.917 --> 00:03:26.393
Be careful! Don't say: She could not be at home.

61
00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:30.565
Say: She might not be at home.

62
00:03:30.865 --> 00:03:32.679
Use might not for a guess.

63
00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:36.154
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:38.444
Maybe, Maybe Not.

65
00:03:38.744 --> 00:03:40.894
My friend might be studying right now.

66
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.259
Or she could be having dinner with her family.

67
00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.765
It may rain later, so take an umbrella.

68
00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.813
I am uncertain, so I use might.

69
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.579
Perhaps she will call us tonight.

70
00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.808
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:02.581
It blank rain tomorrow. I'm not sure.

72
00:04:02.881 --> 00:04:06.000
A, might. B, must. C, has to.

73
00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:11.171
The answer is A: might.

74
00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:14.690
He blank be at home. Perhaps.

75
00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:18.203
A, could. B, can't. C, will.

76
00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.244
The answer is A: could.

77
00:04:24.383 --> 00:04:26.209
Which modal is more formal?

78
00:04:26.509 --> 00:04:29.616
A, may. B, gonna. C, might.

79
00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.108
The answer is A: may.

80
00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.971
Which sentence is a guess?

81
00:04:38.271 --> 00:04:42.842
A, She is at work.. B, She might be at work.. C, She works..

82
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.026
The answer is B: She might be at work..

83
00:04:50.183 --> 00:04:52.821
According to the reading, what should you take?

84
00:04:53.121 --> 00:04:57.053
A, an umbrella. B, a hat. C, a bag.

85
00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.948
The answer is A: an umbrella.

86
00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:07.099
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.994
Write a sentence guessing what a friend might be doing right now.

88
00:05:19.783 --> 00:05:21.260
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:32.621
My friend might be playing football with his brothers, or he could be doing his homework. I am not sure, so I use might and could. Perhaps he is already asleep.

90
00:05:32.921 --> 00:05:34.723
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:35.617 --> 00:05:41.543
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and modals of possibility: might and could and may.

92
00:05:41.843 --> 00:05:45.807
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

93
00:05:46.107 --> 00:05:48.632
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

94
00:05:48.932 --> 00:05:51.619
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

